     The ddvvmmrrppccttll program controls the dvmrpd(8) daemon.  Commands may be ab‐
     breviated to the minimum unambiguous prefix; for example, ss ss for sshhooww
     ssuummmmaarryy.

     The following commands are available:

     lloogg bbrriieeff
             Disable verbose debug logging.

     lloogg vveerrbboossee
             Enable verbose debug logging.

     sshhooww iiggmmpp
             Show IGMP status for all interfaces.

     sshhooww iinntteerrffaacceess [_i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e]
             Show details for all interfaces or the specified _i_n_t_e_r_f_a_c_e.

     sshhooww mmffcc [ddeettaaiill]
             Show the Multicast Forwarding Cache.  ddeettaaiill can be specified for
             additional detail.

     sshhooww nneeiigghhbboorr [ddeettaaiill]
             Show neighbors.  ddeettaaiill can be specified for additional detail.

     sshhooww rriibb [ddeettaaiill]
             Show the Routing Information Base.  ddeettaaiill can be specified for
             additional detail.

     sshhooww ssuummmmaarryy
